{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added a per-feed `fetch_timeout` (integer seconds, 0 = use the global timeout).\n\n- Schema: new migration adds `feeds.fetch_timeout int not null default 0`.\n- Model: `Feed.FetchTimeout` (`fetch_timeout` in the API feed object) and `FeedModificationRequest.FetchTimeout`, applied in `Patch`, so `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}` accepts it.\n- Storage: the column is written in `CreateFeed` and `UpdateFeed` and read in the feed query builder.\n- Refresh: `RefreshFeed` uses the per-feed value when it is above 0, otherwise the global `HTTPClientTimeout`.\n- Validation: a negative value is rejected with a 400. The error message is a plain English string, not a translated locale key.\n- Go client: `FetchTimeout` added to `Feed` and `FeedModificationRequest` in `client/model.go`.\n\nThe existing build, unit tests and integration tests pass (check 1 of 10); nothing exercises the new timeout behaviour itself.\n\nNot done:\n- The override applies only to the feed refresh request. The icon fetch and the scraper/processor requests for that feed still use the global timeout.\n- The field is not accepted on feed creation and is not exposed in the web UI edit form.", "t": 1794464001.337}
